PLAIN-SPEAK QUESTION

A39 found two bad extremes.

One design said:

"my old support makes me somewhat tougher."

It was not tough enough.

The other said:

"I will not really give way
until my whole evidence balance flips."

That was too stubborn.

A40 asks for a middle behavior:

"let my accumulated support
absorb part of this bad pulse.

If the bad pulse is stronger
than the support I have left,
let the leftover pressure
start wearing me down."

The test is whether
that lets a strong core survive a short disturbance
while still letting the organism
change its mind promptly
when the world truly changes.

